Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
what's going on everybody it's warren  welcome back to the cosmic wonder  and today i was so fortunate enough to  attend the black  widow press conference over zoom of  course not in person yet  i can't wait till they start doing them  in person again but it was awesome to  see  scarlett johansson florence pugh david  harbor rachel vice kate shortland and  kevin feige talk about black widow since  we've been waiting for it for such  a long time and the cast really is great  together on  and off screen in the film you can tell  that the cast has a lot of chemistry  with each other which makes for a really  good film so there is a lot to go over  from this press conference and i think  if you are very excited for black widow  you'll enjoy  what the cast had to say i am going to  kind of go out of order of the questions  that were asked during the press  conference because i want to talk about  david harbour specifically because to me  he's kind of the comedy of the film his  character  red guardian is a really good character  and for those of you who may not be  aware i did get to pre-screen black  widow a couple of days ago so i have  seen the film  so sarah spain from espn was the host  and commentator  for this press conference and she asked  david harbour how he establishes the  line between  seriousness and humor and comedy and his  reply was fantastic he  said what's really funny about it is  that it hatches from  the same egg the pathos and also the  humor of this character  he is filled with grief over the choices  that he's made like emotionally  spiritually and nutritiously because  obviously he's not in that good of shape  anymore  but he continues to say that the comedy  itself comes out of the ego  that is built to defend the remorse  that's inherently silly that's  inherently funny so in other words he  says he has to be bombastic because he  can't stop  and feel these things you know all of  his failures so he builds around him  kind of a psychotic world where he  is the hero and that's where he says  that's inherently silly and  inherently funny then he goes on to say  also the family dynamics themselves  are just so fun there's almost a  traditional shot of  us all around a table where we're all in  super suits i found us all falling into  this cliche rolls and then  riffing off them that was really fun and  satisfying as well  and it really is you know you have these  super people you have three black widows  three highly trained assassins and the  red guardian who  is a super soldier you know the russian  captain america and we've all seen this  part in the trailers they  all just kind of sit down and have like  a family moment and it is kind of  inherently funny but it's also a great  emotional scene that adds to the dynamic  of what we're watching as the press  conference continued scarlett johansson  was asked  how she felt to welcome new people to  the marvel family  through the black widow cast in which  she replied it's exciting because i'm  partial  i love our marvel family and i know how  special it is and how special  experiences are making these films so  i'm just excited for other actors to  come in because i know  i hope they all feel similarly it's  wonderful to see people come into things  excited and wide eyes and get to  experience the incredible world of  marvel  and making these huge productions we  have all been a part of big productions  before  but i think because marvel feels so  familial it's just a unique  warm inviting place it's just a fun  thing to share and that says a lot about  marvel and disney you know  huge huge companies huge productions but  at the heart of it all  it's still very warm and welcoming and  calm and i personally think that's why  they can make such good films  just comfortability on the set and in  the writer's room  now i know a lot of people have  personally asked me about the fight  scenes of the film and i do think that  they are really great  i like the hand-to-hand combat that we  see there's one-on-one fights there's  big chase scenes there's group fights  and director kate shortland was asked  that while crafting these fight scenes  if she looked at previous mcu films for  influence on the style  and what she said was different fights  had different hearts to them  say we're looking at the fight on the  bridge with taskmaster she's trying to  use her skill set but the character  she's fighting  he can do what she can do basically  scarlett can't use those skills  what we tried to do in other fights was  to really mess it up  and it became like a street fight with  her sister she's up against a formidable  opponent so those fights became messy  and raw and that was really fun  and i can attest to that those fights  that get messy they are really fun and  they're really awesome to watch  i personally think that the fights to me  were the coolest parts of the film  even between natasha and elena that was  one of the best fights of the film and  i'm glad they put a lot of effort  into understanding what the fight  actually is and i'm glad these fights  did become messy  now a really fun question that was asked  to david harbor and rachel weiss was  which other marvel hero would you like  your character to team up with  david harbour after sarcastically  stating that nobody is on red guardian's  level said that he would love to team up  with anthony mackie's captain america  as we know the red guardian is  essentially the russian captain america  and in the film we learn how he feels  about steve rogers's captain america and  i think a movie  with anthony mackey's captain america  and david harbor's red guardian would be  absolutely hilarious and awesome to  watch i also would really really love  a red guardian solo movie which they  briefly mentioned but didn't really talk  about  david made a joke like kevin are you  listening i don't think there's any  serious talks about this  at marvel studios right now but i for  sure would love to see a red guardian  film  there's a lot of story to tell there in  fact david harper says you have this big  25 year gap that we don't know we don't  know what happened in red guardian's  life  he has all these stories about his life  and what went on they are questionable  about what's real i do think the classic  cold war thing  is a really fun and funny dynamic  between these two guys and the fact that  they basically came up as nuclear  warheads in an arms race together so  again i would love to see that and then  rachel vice said  the hulk which after you see the movie  you can see why this would be a pretty  interesting choice and no i am not  stating that the hulk or bruce banner is  in the movie  they are not now here's a very  interesting question that i think fans  would like to know  kevin feige was asked if we should  expect more prequels and here's what he  said  this film and this story is a particular  case for natasha  but the notion of exploring the past  present and future  of the mcu is certainly in the cards for  all of our characters  which is absolutely fantastic news for  the heroes that don't get their own solo  films and we don't really see the entire  origin story play out  it would be really really cool to see  prequels even for  yelena bulova herself it would be nice  to see a lot more of her experience  in the red room as a black widow the  fact that prequels are on the table for  kevin feige says that there's a lot of  potential for the mcu  then scarlett johansson was asked how  did the story for black widow come about  and i was actually a little bit  surprised with her answer as to when  they decided to do a black widow film  she stated we started talking about this  film as more of a serious possibility  when we were doing  infinity war we already knew what the  end game was for natasha  we wanted to make sure that was a choice  she made actively that it felt like she  had resolved then  so knowing that we had to work backwards  so she could get to a place where that  was possible  we knew that in this film she had to  evolve to a place where she was moving  forward in her life  and had resolved the trauma from her  past that she felt like a different  person  moving forward if that makes sense it  was a very weird way of working  maybe that is always the case with a  prequel i've never done anything like  that  and that makes sense to me to me that's  a very interesting way to approach a  film you already know the characters  in game as she says we know that in  avengers in-game she's going to die so  in black widow  the story is about building up her  character to be  in a good enough place to where  everything about her past is already  taken care of and she feels comfortable  sacrificing herself and that's what  black widow is really about  clearing up those loose ends now i know  a lot of people  are wondering about yelena bulova and  she truly is a great character in this  film florence pew did an amazing job  playing her  and one of the questions that was asked  to florence p was how do you approach  yelena's connection to natasha and make  sure we understand it but  also make elena a character of her own  in what she said  from the get-go it was very obvious that  they have this connection and they have  this relationship and ultimately despite  her skill set  she is that wonderfully annoying younger  sister that says all the right things  at all the wrong times she would go on  to praise director kate shortland for  giving her the freedom to figure out  how elena thinks and how she moves what  she wears  florence says that i think for me that  was such a fun part of this character  she really comes out of the red room and  can start life and she can buy clothes  and she can buy the vest that has a lot  of pockets don't worry that will be  explained  in the movie and she says that she had  so much freedom to discover who elena  was that elena really does become  her own character and does flourish by  the end of the film and she also  complimented scarlett johansson for  being so  welcoming and for being so giving and  really making it a comfortable space  now a big final question that was asked  to scarlett was  what trait does scarlett johansson want  people to remember  about natasha romanov she initially  jokingly responds about her pose but  classic  black widow poses that we've seen her do  throughout the mcu  which the black widow film actually  addresses in a pretty hilarious way  but then on a more serious note she says  i think natasha has a lot of integrity  she's a big character she's not afraid  to admit when she's wrong  she's endearing that way she's curious  about herself and curious about other  people  i think it makes her stand out and it  definitely does  it's an incredible story arc black  widows if you think about it  she goes from being a russian spy and  assassinating people  to a character that has immense  integrity that would eventually go on to  sacrifice herself  to save the people she loves and the  world and it's really great in this  press conference that they really talked  about how much  effort and thought was put into this  movie because again we've waited for a  pretty long  time to get a solo black widow film and  i'm excited for everybody to watch it it  comes out publicly july  9th both on disney plus premiere access  and  in theaters be sure to let me know how  excited you are about the film in the  comments down below and don't forget to  subscribe and hit that notification bell  so you don't miss out on any of the  latest videos  don't forget to like the video and for  live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter as always thank  you all so much for watching  woof  you

